  "rationale": "The key constraints are: (1) throughput >= 32 Msps, (2) max_abs_err <= 2^-12, (3) sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.5us. The batch constraint is critical: 32 requests must all complete within 500ns of the tick. This requires either very high throughput (pipelined, 1/cycle) or high parallelism (unrolled_k with large k). The iterative family is excluded because it produces 1 result every N+3 cycles, giving throughput of Fmax/(N+3) which for N=13 is ~14 Msps at 200MHz, well below 32 Msps, and the batch latency would be 32*(16) cycles = 512 cycles = 2.56us at 200MHz, far exceeding 500ns. For accuracy, N=13-16 iterations with data_width=14-16 should meet the 12-bit constraint. I focus budget on pipelined_m (m=1) and pipelined as they are the most likely to meet all constraints with minimal area, and unrolled_k as a secondary option. angle_guard and frac_guard are set to 0 to minimize area since N=13+ should provide sufficient accuracy without extra guard bits."
