  "rationale": "The exploration has successfully mapped the Pareto front for the `pipelined` family, which is the only architecture capable of meeting the strict system constraints (32 MSPS throughput and 0.5 us p99 batch latency). The `unrolled_k` and `pipelined_m` families were proven infeasible for this spec due to insufficient throughput (max 6.13 and 96.1 MSPS respectively, but failing the batch latency/throughput combination for the 32-request burst). The current front covers the area range from 40,573 um^2 to 76,084 um^2 with accuracy from 12.4 to 17.8 bits. The minimum area feasible design (40,573 um^2) meets all constraints: throughput 138 MSPS >= 32, max_abs_err 0.000187 <= 0.000244, and the pipelined architecture ensures 1 result/cycle, which analytically guarantees the 0.5 us batch latency for 32 requests at ~138 MHz (32 cycles / 138 MHz ≈ 0.23 us < 0.5 us). Since this is the final round and the front is well-defined with a clear minimum-area candidate that satisfies all hard constraints, stopping is the correct decision. The selection rule (min area) will pick the 40,573 um^2 design."
